    "updated_at": "2018-01-25T10:47:54Z",
    "body": "@annevk It is not my topic but I agree that sentence and I think the \"WONTFIX\" should be deleted. \r\n\r\nIn my case of expanded form my client hurts themself in one browser. I want to mark default button \"Save changes\" as default and in many browsers it worked but in part of the default was \"delete item\" or \"add item\" (in context to count of data). Client doesn't notice it frequently but yesterday I have an \"unpleasant\" phone call and request to fix the problem and... entering the deleted data and checked completness of them FOR MY COST due to NOT DEFINED BEHAVIOUR submission with enter key. There should be defined identical behaviour or forbidden ENTER key in text inputs by HTML spec. \r\n\r\nPlease add `default` to mark the default submit button and describe that default button can be only one in each form (+ add it in HTML validator). If no default marked button please describe which button is default. In my opinion if not marked, the last button or with greatest tabindex should be defined. \r\nAdditionally please specify, that after submitting with use of ENTER in text-like fields (password, email, tel, text etc.) the button recognized as default is FOCUSED (not activated) (:focus not :active). They in focused state are often styled with CSS and the user will see which button was selected (it works in IE11 except of `default=\"default\"`).\r\n\r\ntemporarily I can only double the submit button and meet client's requirements but the form in this case will be hard to screen readers but in this case less harmfull is incompletee semantic than correct working in all browsers. \r\n\r\nBTW. All browsers have disabled JavaScript in the client's company due to security policy. I cannot add JS workaround in this case. ",
