    "created_at": "2021-11-06T02:23:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-11-06T02:23:34Z",
    "body": "Hello. I am developing a blog service and its edit page has multiple submit buttons, \"Publish\" and \"Save as Draft\". It is the same situation as the example in `formnovalidate` section of HTML spec.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/form-control-infrastructure.html#attr-fs-formnovalidate\r\n\r\n> ```html\r\n> <form action=\"editor.cgi\" method=\"post\">\r\n>  <p><label>Name: <input required name=fn></label></p>\r\n>  <p><label>Essay: <textarea required name=essay></textarea></label></p>\r\n>  <p><input type=submit name=submit value=\"Submit essay\"></p>\r\n>  <p><input type=submit formnovalidate name=save value=\"Save essay\"></p>\r\n>  <p><input type=submit formnovalidate name=cancel value=\"Cancel\"></p>\r\n> </form>\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nIn such situations, the button which I want to mark as default may not appear first in document order.  I think it is helpful if we can mark a certain button as default.",
